  RecentChargesSection is the Recent Charges section of the Vehicle Detail page: a GlassPanel with
  a green BatteryCharging "Recent Charges" header (+ a "View all" → /charging link) over either a
  charging-sessions DataTable (when there is at least one session) or an EmptyState ("No charging
  sessions recorded yet"). The native surface reproduces its data, composition, every state, and
  i18n keys via shared P1/S8 state-holder seams (no view I/O):

  Composition (web → native), all FIVE useChargeColumns cells reproduced VERBATIM (not stubbed):
   1. Date     — formatDateTime(s.start_ts): locale year·abbrev-month·day·hour·minute, "—" if
                 nil/invalid (web `if (!iso || isNaN) return '—'`).
   2. Energy   — `${fmtNumber(convertEnergyFromSI(total_energy_added_wh ?? 0,'kWh'))} kWh`: SI Wh
                 → kWh (÷1000) at the GLOBAL number precision (fmtNumber default = 2) + " kWh".
                 SORTABLE (web `sortable: true`) — the native column carries a numeric comparator
                 on the underlying SI Wh, so sorting orders by value, not the "X kWh" text.
   3. Duration — durationStr(duration_min): h = floor(min/60) raw, m = fmtInt(min % 60),
                 `{h}h {m}m` / `{m}m`.
   4. Cost     — `cost != null ? formatCurrency(cost) : '—'`: currency symbol + fmtNumber at the
                 USER precision (settings.decimal_precision ?? 2), else the em-dash.
   5. Battery  — `end_soc_pct != null ? "{start}% → {end}%" : "{start}%"`, the SOC numbers
                 interpolated JS-style (no grouping, integers without a fraction).

  Energy pipeline ported VERBATIM from lib/unitConversion.ts + lib/numberFormat.ts:
  convertEnergyFromSI (Wh → kWh = wh/1000) + fmtNumber (grouped, locale-aware, half-up; default
  precision 2). SI Wh is read directly from the seam; the kWh conversion happens only at the cell
  (web useUnits / display boundary), honouring the frontend SI cutover. Cost uses the user
  precision (web useFormatting) distinct from the energy global precision; both default to 2.

  DataTable parity: web `<DataTable compact pagination …>` → the shared `TSDataTable(density:
  .compact)` with the five `TSColumn`s (energy sortable). Pagination is the shared table
